{
  "id": "psychotherapeutic-process",
  "term": "psychotherapeutic process",
  "definition": "In this packet, the psychotherapeutic process means the ongoing course of a person’s engagement in psychotherapy as they work with experiences, beliefs, emotions, and habits in ways that can support meaningful change over time. In group psychotherapy, it includes added layers of engagement created through interactions with both the therapist and other group members.",
